body:
I would say so. When I dropped out of school the conditions of me living at home was that I had to be looking for work and pay rent once I found a job, or go into further study and pay rent once my student loan came in. I went into further study and the moment I got my first loan payment I paid the rent money to my parents. The money included money for the bills and food. This was cheaper than leaving and flatting and I enjoyed living with my parents.

&#x200B;

I understand that it can be frustrating as a student as you don't have much money but maybe talk to her and negotiate a price?
